# SPDX-License-Identifier: commercial
#
# Bench HIL-0 on the ESP32-P4 PoE board (docs/multi-arch/esp32-p4-design.md
# §4, docs/development/bench/esp32-p4.md "HIL-0"). Passed as
# ESP_SDKCONFIG_EXTRA, which applies after this board's sdkconfig.defaults:
#
#   make esp32-build BOARD=esp32p4-poe CRYPTO=none \
#        ESP_SDKCONFIG_EXTRA=boards/esp32p4-poe/sdkconfig.hil0
#
# HIL-0 writes no eFuse, and either of these would burn some on first boot:
# ESP-IDF secure boot v2 its key digest, flash encryption its key and
# counter. Both are off.
#
# The app is still built signed, with no secure boot on the part:
# "Require signed app images" without hardware secure boot builds it with
# --secure-pad-v2 and signs it with the same RSA key as the release, so
# boot/hal/esp32/l0_seal.py finds the zero segment it grows for the trailer
# (it refuses any other image) and re-signs the sealed app. The bootloader is
# not signed, so the ROM does not check it and ESP-IDF's bootloader does not
# check the app's RSA signature (SECURE_SIGNED_ON_BOOT_NO_SECURE_BOOT off).
#
# The check that runs is not a Kconfig setting: layer 0's ES256 check of the
# app's trailer v1 against the key pin in tfw_plat is built into the
# bootloader, and nothing here turns it off (CA m453: there is no
# BOOT_SIG=none). The tier is not Kconfig either: CRYPTO=none picks the object
# list, and with no HMAC_UP key in eFuse layer 0 hands off tier none.
CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT=n
CONFIG_SECURE_FLASH_ENC_ENABLED=n
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_NO_SECURE_BOOT=y
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_RSA_SCHEME=y
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_ON_BOOT_NO_SECURE_BOOT=n
CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT_BUILD_SIGNED_BINARIES=y
